 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Low-frequency lighting:** Creates large regions where the error function is close to zero with very small gradients, dominated by Monte Carlo or measurement noise. Standard SGD gets trapped here [S1].
-*   **Local Minima:** Solutions found in low-error regions under low-frequency lighting may generalize poorly to high-frequency lighting [S1].
-*   **Physical Validity:** Parameters $g$ and $\sigma_s$ must remain within physical bounds (e.g., $\sigma_s > 0$, $g \in [-1, 1]$) [G].
+*   **Low-frequency lighting:** Creates large regions where the error function $d(g, \sigma_s)$ is close to zero with very small gradients, dominated by Monte Carlo or measurement noise, trapping SGD [S1].
+*   **Local Minima:** Solutions found in low-error regions under low-frequency lighting generalize poorly to high-frequency lighting [S1].
+*   **Physical Validity:** Parameters $g$ and $\sigma_s$ must remain within physical bounds ($\sigma_s > 0$, $g \in [-1, 1]$) [G].
 
